    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d769">

                <pb facs="0667" n="655" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg655"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890D.01/626</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Under Secretary of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-08-04">August 4, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Monsieur Tixier called to see me this afternoon at his request.</p>
                <p>[Here follows paragraph dealing with the appointment of American Consul General
                    to Brazzaville; see <ref target="frus:frus1942v02/pg_557">volume II, pages
                        557</ref> ff.]</p>
                <p>Monsieur Tixier then raised the question of Syria. He stated that he understood
                    that the Government of the United States intended appointing a new Diplomatic
                    Agent and Consul General in Syria, and he was instructed to request that this
                    action should not be taken before the United States accorded recognition to
                    Syria and the Lebanon as independent states. He said he understood, however,
                    that this Government was not yet prepared to take such a step and he asked if
                    this Government would not therefore be willing to adopt the same procedure as
                    that indicated above in this instance, and let the competent authorities in
                    Syria and the Lebanon have a copy of the commission of the American Diplomatic
                    Agent and Consul General for their information. I said I would be glad also to
                    have consideration given to this suggestion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S[<hi rendition="#small-caps">umner</hi>] W[<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >elles</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
